      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was renamed Irvine to honor Colonel William Irvine, a Revolutionary War officer who helped Kentucky statehood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Irvine,_Kentucky",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The railroad arrived in 1869 via Kentucky Central Railway, boosting trade of timber and crops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
